  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lar gibbon protection in the Western Forest Complex, Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to protect and potentially increase the population of lar gibbon in the Huai Kha Khaeng Wildlife Sanctuary. The main objectives of this project are to maintain the SMART (Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool) patrol system in Huai Kha Khaeng to the current intensity and coverage, and to establish a baseline population estimate for lar gibbon in HKK. The following activities will be accomplished: (a) conduct close follow-up monitoring with 22 patrol teams (5 rangers/team) in Huai Kha Khaeng Wildlife Sanctuary by providing technical support, refresher training, necessary equipment, patrol ration costs, and other morale boosting activities, (b) conduct a population estimate by dispatching teams of three observers to selected listening areas that exhibit topographical features known to be of preference to lar gibbon, and carefully selecting listening posts that provide optimal data collection based on surrounding topography, and (c) after five months of data collection there will be a period of data entry and statistical analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
